  "judge_reasoning": "## Evaluation\n\n**Task:** Identify the character in Unicode range 9632 to 9650 that represents a hollow parallelogram.\n\n**Analysis of the screenshots:**\n\n1. **Screenshot 1:** Wolfram Alpha homepage — starting point of the task.\n\n2. **Screenshots 2–3:** The query \"unicode 9632 to 9650\" was entered. Wolfram Alpha interpreted it as \"Unicode (character set) 9632 to 9650\" and displayed the Geometric Shapes characters from U+25A0 through U+25B2. In the last row, U+25B0 appears as a filled (black) parallelogram and U+25B1 appears as an outlined (hollow) parallelogram, followed by U+25B2 (filled triangle). This confirms the range contains a hollow parallelogram at U+25B1.\n\n3. **Screenshots 4–5:** The follow-up query \"unicode U+25B1\" was entered. Wolfram Alpha shows:\n   - Input interpretation: character 9649\n   - Visual form: a hollow parallelogram outline\n   - Name: \"white parallelogram\"\n   - Encodings: Unicode U+25B1 (decimal: 9649)\n   - Unicode block: Geometric Shapes (9632 through 9727)\n\n**Verification of correctness:**\n- Decimal 9632 = U+25A0 and decimal 9650 = U+25B2, so U+25B1 (decimal 9649) falls within the specified range. ✓\n- \"White parallelogram\" is the hollow/outline version (vs. U+25B0 \"black parallelogram,\" which is filled), matching the \"hollow parallelogram\" description. ✓\n- The visual form in the screenshots clearly shows a hollow parallelogram outline for U+25B1. ✓\n\n**Result Response consistency:** The response states the answer is U+25B1 WHITE PARALLELOGRAM (decimal 9649), verified via Wolfram Alpha with both queries. This matches the screenshots exactly.\n\nThe task was fully accomplished: the correct character was identified and verified with supporting evidence from the screenshots.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
